---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Flash sale: 100 units, 1,000 buyers" hint="Compare four ways of taking the stock. All four see the same buyers, and some of them abandon the purchase. Watch for sold units that do not exist, units that sit unsold, and who got in out of order.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>At the <b>start values</b> (100 buyers per step, 30% abandon, cart hold 12), <b>decrement after payment</b> collects money for <b>363</b> units and <b>263</b> of them do not exist. <b>Reserve at the cart</b> sells only <b>76</b>, leaving <b>24 units unsold</b> although <b>651</b> buyers were told "sold out". The <b>queue</b> sells all <b>100</b> and nobody jumps the line.</li>
    <li>Set the <b>abandon rate to 0</b>: the three reserving designs all sell 100, because nobody leaves a hold behind. Decrement-after-payment still oversells (<b>300</b> too many), since it only learns the stock after the payments arrive.</li>
    <li>Back at the start values (30% abandon), set the <b>cart hold to 4</b>, the same as the time to pay: the unsold units fall from 24 to <b>1</b>. A long hold is the price of reserving early. The queue never needs to guess, but its last unit is sold later (step <b>34</b>, against step 5 to 12 for the others), because it waits for the abandoned holds to run out.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg ecb" data-ecb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Buyers arriving per step <input type="range" min="10" max="200" step="10" value="100" data-a /> <b data-aval></b></label>
      <label>Buyers who never pay (%) <input type="range" min="0" max="60" step="5" value="30" data-ab /> <b data-abval></b></label>
      <label>Cart hold before it expires (steps) <input type="range" min="4" max="30" value="12" data-ttl /> <b data-ttlval></b></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Decrement after payment</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span><span class="pg-note" data-m1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Reserve at the cart, with expiry</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span><span class="pg-note" data-m2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Atomic decrement at checkout, then pay</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span><span class="pg-note" data-m3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Queue in front of the stock</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span><span class="pg-note" data-m4></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: 100 units, 1,000 buyers who arrive in order, a fixed number per step. Paying takes 4 steps after the buyer gets a claim. A buyer who is told "sold out" leaves for good. 1: any buyer who arrives while fewer than 100 payments have completed goes on to pay, and the first 100 payments get the units. 2: the unit is taken at once and held for the cart hold, or until paid. 3: the same, but the hold lasts only 6 steps, as for a payment window. 4: buyers wait in arrival order, and are let in only as long as units are free (at most 20 per step), and every hold lasts 6 steps. "Jumped the line" counts buyers who got a unit although a genuine buyer who arrived in an earlier step was turned away.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-ecb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const S = 100; const B = 1000; const PAY = 4; const HOLD = 6; const ADM = 20;
    const SEED = 77; const MAX_STEPS = 400; // safety cap on the queue simulation
    let seed = SEED; const rnd = () => ((seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296) / 4294967296);
    const draws = Array.from({ length: B }, () => rnd());
    type R = { sold: number; over: number; unsold: number; falseOut: number; jumpers: number; last: number; wait: number; paid: number };
    type Hold = { i: number; t: number; pays: boolean };
    function run(A: number, ab: number, ttl: number): R[] {
      const gone = draws.map((d) => d < ab); // true: this buyer never pays
      const arr = Array.from({ length: B }, (_, i) => Math.floor(i / A));
      const lastArr = arr[B - 1];
      const jumpers = (honored: number[], denied: number[]) => { const m = denied.length ? Math.min(...denied.map((i) => arr[i])) : Infinity; return honored.filter((i) => arr[i] > m).length; };
      const out: R[] = [];
      // 1. Check the stock at checkout, decrement when the payment arrives.
      { const pays: { i: number; t: number }[] = []; const turned: number[] = []; const due: Record<number, number> = {}; let paid = 0;
        for (let t = 0; t <= lastArr + PAY; t++) {
          paid += due[t] || 0;
          if (t <= lastArr) for (let i = t * A; i < Math.min(B, (t + 1) * A); i++) {
            if (paid < S) { if (!gone[i]) { pays.push({ i, t: t + PAY }); due[t + PAY] = (due[t + PAY] || 0) + 1; } } else turned.push(i);
          }
        }
        pays.sort((a, b) => a.t - b.t || a.i - b.i);
        const honored = pays.slice(0, S).map((p) => p.i);
        const denied = [...turned.filter((i) => !gone[i]), ...pays.slice(S).map((p) => p.i)];
        out.push({ sold: honored.length, over: pays.length - honored.length, paid: pays.length, unsold: S - honored.length, falseOut: 0, jumpers: jumpers(honored, denied), last: honored.length ? pays[honored.length - 1].t : 0, wait: 0 }); }
      // 2 and 3. Take the unit at once and give it back when the hold runs out.
      for (const hold of [ttl, HOLD]) {
        let holds: Hold[] = []; const sold: number[] = []; const turned: number[] = []; let falseOut = 0; let last = 0;
        for (let t = 0; t <= lastArr + hold + PAY; t++) {
          holds = holds.filter((h) => { if (h.pays && t >= h.t + PAY) { sold.push(h.i); last = t; return false; } if (!h.pays && t >= h.t + hold) return false; return true; });
          if (t <= lastArr) for (let i = t * A; i < Math.min(B, (t + 1) * A); i++) {
            if (S - sold.length - holds.length > 0) holds.push({ i, t, pays: !gone[i] });
            else { turned.push(i); if (!gone[i] && holds.some((h) => !h.pays)) falseOut++; }
          }
        }
        out.push({ sold: sold.length, over: 0, paid: sold.length, unsold: S - sold.length, falseOut, jumpers: jumpers(sold, turned.filter((i) => !gone[i])), last, wait: 0 });
      }
      // 4. A queue admits buyers in arrival order, only as fast as units become free.
      { const queue: number[] = []; let holds: Hold[] = []; const sold: number[] = []; let last = 0; let wait = 0;
        for (let t = 0; t < MAX_STEPS; t++) {
          holds = holds.filter((h) => { if (h.pays && t >= h.t + PAY) { sold.push(h.i); last = t; return false; } if (!h.pays && t >= h.t + HOLD) return false; return true; });
          if (t <= lastArr) for (let i = t * A; i < Math.min(B, (t + 1) * A); i++) queue.push(i);
          const n = Math.min(S - sold.length - holds.length, ADM, queue.length);
          for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) { const i = queue.shift() as number; holds.push({ i, t, pays: !gone[i] }); if (!gone[i]) wait = Math.max(wait, t - arr[i]); }
          if (sold.length === S || (queue.length === 0 && holds.length === 0 && t > lastArr)) break;
        }
        out.push({ sold: sold.length, over: 0, paid: sold.length, unsold: S - sold.length, falseOut: 0, jumpers: jumpers(sold, queue.filter((i) => !gone[i])), last, wait }); }
      return out;
    }
    const f = (n: number) => n.toLocaleString('en-US');
    function draw() {
      const A = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-a]').value); const ab = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-ab]').value) / 100; const ttl = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-ttl]').value);
      q('[data-aval]').textContent = String(A); q('[data-abval]').textContent = String(Math.round(ab * 100)); q('[data-ttlval]').textContent = String(ttl);
      const r = run(A, ab, ttl);
      r.forEach((x, i) => {
        const k = i + 1;
        q(`[data-o${k}]`).textContent = x.over > 0 ? `${x.sold} delivered, ${f(x.over)} oversold` : `${x.sold} of ${S} units sold`;
        q(`[data-n${k}]`).textContent = x.over > 0 ? `${f(x.paid)} buyers paid for ${S} units, and ${f(x.over)} must be refunded`
          : x.unsold > 0 ? `${x.unsold} ${x.unsold === 1 ? 'unit' : 'units'} left unsold${x.falseOut > 0 ? `, while ${f(x.falseOut)} buyers were told "sold out"` : ''}`
          : i === 3 ? `longest wait in the queue: ${x.wait} steps` : x.falseOut > 0 ? `${f(x.falseOut)} buyers were told "sold out" while abandoned holds still had stock` : 'every unit sold';
        q(`[data-m${k}]`).textContent = `jumped the line: ${f(x.jumpers)}. Last unit settled at step ${x.last}`;
        const bad = x.over > 0 || x.unsold > 0 || x.jumpers > 0;
        q<HTMLElement>(`[data-b${k}]`).style.setProperty('--c', bad ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      });
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); const bad = r[0].over > 0 || r[1].unsold > 0 || r[2].unsold > 0 || r[1].jumpers + r[2].jumpers > 0; out.classList.toggle('bad', bad);
      const parts: string[] = [];
      if (r[0].over > 0) parts.push(`Decrement-after-payment collected money for ${f(r[0].paid)} units when there were ${S}: ${f(r[0].over)} orders were oversold, because every buyer who arrived before the first payments finished still saw stock.`);
      const worst = r[1].unsold >= r[2].unsold ? r[1] : r[2];
      if (worst.unsold > 0) parts.push(`Reserving early left ${worst.unsold} units unsold at the end: abandoned holds kept the page at "sold out" until they expired, and by then the buyers had gone.`);
      if (r[1].jumpers + r[2].jumpers > 0) parts.push(`Because returned units go to whoever arrives next, ${Math.max(r[1].jumpers, r[2].jumpers)} buyers got in ahead of earlier buyers who had been turned away.`);
      if (r[3].sold === S && r[3].jumpers === 0) parts.push(`The queue sold all ${S} units in arrival order with no oversell, but its last unit was settled at step ${r[3].last}${ab > 0 ? ', because it waits for abandoned holds to expire instead of guessing' : ''}.`);
      out.textContent = parts.length ? parts.join(' ') : 'With these settings every design sells the stock exactly once. Raise the arrival rate or the abandon rate to see the others fail.';
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
